It really is the most lovely building you'll ever see.

110
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:02,940
I mean, it's over...

111
00:06:06,150 --> 00:06:07,610
Oh, my God.

112
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:10,610
It's nice.

113
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Oh. Oh, my God.

114
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:24,420
How can this be happening? What are we gonna do?

115
00:06:24,590 --> 00:06:26,510
Everything's gonna be all right.

116
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:29,970
How is it gonna be all right?

117
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:29,970
Uh-huh, I see that.

118
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,300
Okay, I talked to the guy and found out what happened.

119
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:35,810
What?

120
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:35,810
They tore it down a few days early.

121
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:41,810
All right.

122
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,020
Westminster Abbey.

123
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:46,780
Hands down, best abbey I ever seen.

124
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,360
Hey.

125
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:50,820
Okay.

126
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:53,030
What do you think of the abbey, Chandler?

127
00:06:53,870 --> 00:06:57,040
Oh, I think it's great. They're thinking of changing the name.

128
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:00,410
Really? To what?

129
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:00,410
To "Put the Camera Away."

130
00:07:01,670 --> 00:07:04,460
Man, you are Westminster Crabby.

131
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:15,550
Honey, don't get up. What do you need?

132
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:15,550
Oh, no. Oh, nothing.

133
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:18,930
Come on. I'm here to take care of you. What do you need? Anything.

134
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:20,980
Okay, I have a wedgie.

135
00:07:23,690 --> 00:07:24,940
Okay, that is all you.

136
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:30,150
So, what do you want for lunch?

137
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:32,360
Oh, I don't know.

138
00:07:32,530 --> 00:07:35,820
I guess we have to eat.

139
00:07:32,530 --> 00:07:35,820
Yeah, I do.

140
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:38,620
What's the matter?

141
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:41,620
I'm just bummed the way I left things with Ross.

142
00:07:41,790 --> 00:07:44,080
I wish I didn't lie to him about having to work.

143
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:45,670
He seemed so mad at me.

144
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:49,590
Ah, don't be so hard on yourself. If someone I was still in love with was...

145
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:52,670
Still in love with?

146
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:52,670
Yeah.

147
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,260
I'm not in love with Ross.

148
00:07:55,050 --> 00:07:56,090
Oh.

149
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,220
No, no. Good.

150
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:01,980
Yeah, me neither.

151
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:06,190
Phoebe, I'm not going to Ross' wedding, because he's my ex-boyfriend...

152
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:09,150
...and that would be really uncomfortable.

153
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:13,650
Not because I'm still in love with him. Hey, I like Ross as much as the next guy.

154
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:17,450
You know, clearly I have feelings for him, but feelings don't mean love.

155
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:20,790
You know, I mean, do I still have loving feelings for Ross?

156
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,700
Yeah.

157
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:25,750
I have continuing feelings of love.

158
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,540
But that doesn't mean that I'm still in love with him.

159
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:32,460
You know, I mean, I have sexual feelings for him, but I do love him.

160
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:37,760
Oh, my God. Oh, my...

161
00:08:37,930 --> 00:08:39,850
Why didn't you tell me?

162
00:08:41,470 --> 00:08:43,810
We thought you knew.

163
00:08:41,470 --> 00:08:43,810
We?

164
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:47,060
Yeah, we all know. We talk about it all the time.

165
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:50,520
You all know? Does Ross know?

166
00:08:50,690 --> 00:08:53,650
Oh, no. Ross doesn't know anything.

167
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:55,700
Oh. I cannot believe you didn't tell me.

168
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:58,700
Because we thought you knew. It's so obvious.

169
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:01,700
God, it would be like, you know, telling Monica:

170
00:09:01,870 --> 00:09:04,200
"Hey," you know, "you like things clean."

171
00:09:08,210 --> 00:09:09,250
Hi.

172
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:11,670
So, what are you fine gentlemen in the market for?

173
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:16,470
We've got scarves, souvenir postcards.

174
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:16,470
Check this out, huh?

175
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:18,390
Oh, yeah.

176
00:09:18,550 --> 00:09:20,850
That's the stuff. What do you think?

177
00:09:21,010 --> 00:09:24,390
Well, I'm not gonna have to buy that "I'm with stupid" T-shirt anymore.

178
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:27,940
Well, I like it. Here you go.

179
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:31,860
You're not really gonna buy that. Don't you think you've embarrassed me enough?

180
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:33,480
Oh, I embarrass you?

181
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:36,700
How can I answer that when I'm pretending I don't know you?

182
00:09:37,530 --> 00:09:40,490
He's just jealous. You'll fit right in. All Londoners wear them.

183
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:44,830
Oh, really? Then how come no one here anywhere is wearing one?

184
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,250
They're all tourists.

185
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:51,420
All right, look, if you insist on wearing that in public, you know...

186
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:55,170
...you're gonna spend the rest of the afternoon all by yourself.

187
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:56,970
Oh, yeah?

188
00:10:00,930 --> 00:10:04,310
If you're gonna make me choose between you and the hat, I choose the hat.

189
00:10:04,470 --> 00:10:05,520
Good choice.

190
00:10:04,470 --> 00:10:05,520
Thanks.

191
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,730
Okay, look. All right, that's it, okay?

192
00:10:07,890 --> 00:10:11,190
I'm out of here. I'm not gonna be embarrassed anymore.

193
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,490
Hello?

194
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,490
Hey.

195
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:24,700
I just spoke to your dad, and you know what?

196
00:10:24,870 --> 00:10:27,080
He thinks we'll be able to find a new place.

197
00:10:27,250 --> 00:10:30,000
We don't have to.

198
00:10:27,250 --> 00:10:30,000
What, you found a place?

199
00:10:30,170 --> 00:10:33,420
No, but Monica and I were talking...

200
00:10:33,590 --> 00:10:36,760
...and I was so upset about the hall being knocked down...

201
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:39,970
...and she suggested that we just put the wedding off for a bit.

202
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:45,930
She said what?

203
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:45,930
She said if I'm not happy...

204
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:49,980
...getting married somewhere we can find in a day, well, we should just postpone it.

205
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:54,360
Postpone it? Heh.

206
00:10:56,070 --> 00:11:00,320
Emily, do you think Monica realizes how much our parents spent on this wedding?

207
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:05,030
Huh? Do you think my sister's teeny, tiny little brain comprehends...

208
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,620
...that people took time out of their lives...

209
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:10,710
...to fly thousands of miles to be here? Huh?

210
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,040
This isn't right.

211
00:11:17,130 --> 00:11:19,460
I realize that people are gonna be disappointed.

212
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:23,010
But they'll come back when we can do it right.

213
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,680
Well, I can't ask people to do that. Would you ask people to do that?

214
00:11:26,850 --> 00:11:28,430
Don't you point your pants at me.

215
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,980
We have no choice.

216
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:35,060
Anywhere that's half-decent will have been booked months ago.

217
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:37,770
Ross, don't you understand? This is our wedding.

218
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:40,860
The only thing I understand is postponing it is not an option.

219
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:42,650
This is when we're getting married.

220
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:45,950
What are you saying, it's now or never?

221
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:45,950
No, I'm saying it's now.

222
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:48,540
Or?

223
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:48,540
There's no "or" in mine.

224
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:50,620
What is wrong with these pants?

225
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,790
It's not the pants. It's you who's backwards.

226
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:59,130
And if you don't understand how important this is to me...

227
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,590
...perhaps we shouldn't be getting married at all.

228
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:04,010
Emily, no. Wait, stop. Emily, please...

229
00:12:13,890 --> 00:12:15,810
Hey.

230
00:12:13,890 --> 00:12:15,810
Hi.

231
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:19,110
So did shopping help you feel any better about Ross?

232
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:22,150
Manhattan does not have enough stores.

233
00:12:23,570 --> 00:12:25,950
Well, I think I can help you get over him.

234
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,450
You can?

235
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,450
Yeah.

236
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:30,200
I just need you to bring me some photos of Ross...

237
00:12:30,370 --> 00:12:33,080
...and, um, a small piece of chocolate...

238
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:35,250
...and a glass of tepid water.

239
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:39,670
Ooh. Is this one of those things where you throw stuff in a bag with graveyard dirt...

240
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,880
...and hang it from a north-facing tree?

241
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:44,630
Uh, only if you have the hiccups too.

242
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,510
The pictures are for you. The chocolate and water's for me.

243
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:51,510
I just didn't feel like getting up.

244
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:55,640
Okay. I'm gonna show you a picture of Ross, okay...

245
00:12:55,810 --> 00:12:59,190
...and you're going to remember all the bad things about him, all right?

246
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:01,820
Really focus on his flaws.

247
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:01,820
I can do that.

248
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:04,530
Certainly did that while we were going out. Heh.

249
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,860
Okay. Mm.

250
00:13:06,030 --> 00:13:09,370
Before we get started, I just wanna say, for the record, I love Ross.

251
00:13:09,530 --> 00:13:11,280
I think he's such a great guy.

252
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,330
Okay. Now close your eyes.

253
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:21,670
And imagine that you're with Ross.

254
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:21,670
Mm-hm.

255
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:24,670
Okay, and imagine that you're kissing him.

256
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:24,670
Mm-hm.

257
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:27,880
You're running your hands all over his body.

258
00:13:28,050 --> 00:13:30,600
And then you run your hands through his hair...

259
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:34,810
...but, oh, ew, gross, it's some kind of grease, it's... Ugh.

260
00:13:35,890 --> 00:13:37,060
Ah?

261
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,060
I don't know.

262
00:13:40,230 --> 00:13:42,980
I don't know, his hair never bothered me that much.

263
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:46,820
And you know, it was always more crunchy than it was greasy.

264
00:13:47,450 --> 00:13:50,030
Okay. This is gonna be harder than I thought.

265
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:53,200
Um, ahem. Let's try some aversion therapy.

266
00:13:53,370 --> 00:13:54,950
Okay. All right.

267
00:13:53,370 --> 00:13:54,950
Okay? All right.

268
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,410
Look at the picture.

269
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,410
Okay.

270
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:58,410
All right, and, um...

271
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:01,540
Ow!

272
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:08,970
Okay. How do you feel now?

273
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:08,970
Well, I like you less.

274
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,110
Hey.

275
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,110
Hey.

276
00:14:28,950 --> 00:14:32,620
Oh. Sorry.

277
00:14:28,950 --> 00:14:32,620
No, no, you know what? I'm sorry.

278
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:35,030
I shouldn't have said you were embarrassing me.

279
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,490
That really wasn't cool.

280
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:40,790
And if it makes you feel any better, I've had a really lousy day.

281
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:43,380
Me too.

282
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,250
Yeah?

283
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,250
No!

284
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,670
I had the best day ever.

285
00:14:50,090 --> 00:14:52,680
Dude, check this out.

286
00:14:56,970 --> 00:14:59,230
Say hi to my friend and tell him you like my hat.

287
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:02,440
Okay, so, what's your friend's name?

288
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:02,440
Oh. Chandler.

289
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:03,690
Hi, Chandler.

290
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:05,650
That's... That's...

291
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:08,150
Oh, my God.

292
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:08,150
That's Fergie, baby!

293
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:14,320
Joey says you don't really like his hat, but I think it's kind of dashing.

294
00:15:14,990 --> 00:15:16,280
When did you...? How...?

295
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:19,160
I was trying to figure out how to get to Buckingham Palace.

296
00:15:19,330 --> 00:15:20,710
So I'm in my map and...

297
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:24,500
Hey.

298
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:24,500
Hey.

299
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:26,750
I understand you had a little talk with Emily.

300
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,590
Ha, ha. Yes, I did.

301
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:32,300
And you are welcome.

302
00:15:33,430 --> 00:15:35,260
Am I?

303
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:38,810
And was it your idea to postpone the wedding?

304
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:44,520
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

305
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:44,520
Wait up.

306
00:15:46,230 --> 00:15:50,530
Hey, hey, since you're the fix-it lady, here's a pickle:

307
00:15:50,690 --> 00:15:54,950
What do you do when the bride says she doesn't wanna have the wedding at all?

308
00:15:55,530 --> 00:15:57,240
She said that?

309
00:15:55,530 --> 00:15:57,240
Yeah.

310
00:15:57,410 --> 00:15:58,830
Why?

311
00:15:57,410 --> 00:15:58,830
I don't know.

312
00:15:58,990 --> 00:16:02,710
I told her it was stupid to put off the wedding just because the hall was gone...

313
00:16:02,870 --> 00:16:05,000
...and she, like, flipped out.

314
00:16:05,170 --> 00:16:08,590
Oh, my God. You're even dumber than I am.

315
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:11,710
Excuse me?

316
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:14,880
Ross, how long have you been planning this wedding?

317
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:16,180
I don't know. A month?

318
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:19,760
Emily has probably been planning it since she was 5.

319
00:16:19,930 --> 00:16:23,430
Ever since the first time she took a pillowcase and hung it off her head.

320
00:16:25,230 --> 00:16:27,270
That's what we did.

321
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:30,690
We dreamed about the perfect wedding.

322
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:33,570
In the perfect place.

323
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:36,910
With the perfect four-tiered wedding cake.

324
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,530
With the little people on top.

325
00:16:49,170 --> 00:16:51,920
But the most important part...

326
00:16:52,090 --> 00:16:54,670
...is that we had the perfect guy...

327
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:58,760
...who understood just how important all that other stuff was.

328
00:17:00,850 --> 00:17:02,930
I had no idea.

329
00:17:03,810 --> 00:17:08,020
That pillowcase thing, I thought you guys were just doing The Flying Nun.

330
00:17:10,230 --> 00:17:12,150
Sometimes we were.

331
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,740
Come on.

332
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:17,780
You gotta help me figure out what to do.

333
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:18,990
Okay?

334
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:18,990
All right.

335
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:20,580
Come on.

336
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:27,210
Whoa. Pretty intense, huh?

337
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:27,210
Yeah.

338
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:32,420
I hope Ross didn't think we went in there because we were uncomfortable out here.

339
00:17:38,970 --> 00:17:40,220
I hope he did.

340
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,310
Hello?

341
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,310
Hey, Pheebs, it's Joey.

342
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:52,860
Hey, Joey. Hey. Ooh, ooh.

343
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,860
I just saw someone that looks just like you on the subway.

344
00:17:56,030 --> 00:18:00,490
I was gonna go over and say hi, but then I figured he doesn't care he looks like you.

345
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:04,540
That just cost me 4 bucks.

346
00:18:05,290 --> 00:18:08,540
I just called to see how the chick and the duck are doing.

347
00:18:08,710 --> 00:18:10,790
They're having a great time with Aunt Phoebe.

348
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:13,380
Aunt Rachel hasn't been helpful at all.

349
00:18:14,210 --> 00:18:15,590
So do you miss me?

350
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:18,590
Kind of, but I've just been having way too much fun.

351
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,260
Oh, so you're not homesick yet?

352
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:23,890
No, I don't think so.

353
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:26,390
All right, well, the seven of us miss you.

354
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:32,310
Who's seven?

355
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:32,310
Well, you know, me, Rachel...

356
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,860
...the birds, the babies.

357
00:18:34,020 --> 00:18:36,690
Aw, the babies miss me?

358
00:18:38,610 --> 00:18:41,490
Ooh, pizza guy's here.

359
00:18:38,610 --> 00:18:41,490
What? You ordered pizza without me?

360
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:46,160
Yeah, but we were thinking about you. We ordered the Joey Special.

361
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:48,000
Two pizzas?

362
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:53,790
Yeah. Okay, gotta go. Talk to you later.

363
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:53,790
Wait, wait. Where did you get it from?

364
00:19:00,510 --> 00:19:03,680
Where everybody knows your name

365
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:09,390
And they're always glad you came

366
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:15,520
You wanna be where you can see The troubles are all the same

367
00:19:15,690 --> 00:19:19,530
You wanna be Where everybody knows your name

368
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:28,330
Monica, why have you brought me here?

369
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:28,330
You'll see.

370
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,460
I tell you, this wedding is not gonna happen.

371
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:34,830
Oh, Ross.

372
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:41,510
Okay? But imagine a lot more lights, okay, and, you know, fewer bricks...

373
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:43,590
...and flowers and candles.

374
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:46,600
Okay, and the musicians, they can go over here, okay?

375
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,060
And the chairs, they can face this way and...

376
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,230
You go.

377
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:54,810
But if you don't love this, then we'll do it any other place...

378
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:56,020
...any other time.

379
00:19:56,190 --> 00:19:59,440
Really, it's fine. Whatever you want.

380
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,740
It's perfect.

381
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:07,160
And, I don't know, if it starts to rain...

382
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:07,160
Well, then we'll get wet.

383
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:14,960
I don't even have a date.

384
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,130
Pheebs?

385
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,130
Yeah?

386
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:21,340
Do you remember where the duck food is?

387
00:20:21,510 --> 00:20:24,260
Yeah, it's in the guys' apartment, under the sink. Why?

388
00:20:24,430 --> 00:20:26,470
Because I'm going to London.

389
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:28,890
What? What do you mean, you're going to London?

390
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:31,020
Yeah, I have to tell Ross that I love him.

391
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:34,810
Now, honey, you take care, and you don't have those babies till I get back. Mwah.

392
00:20:35,690 --> 00:20:37,730
Rachel, you can't go. Ross loves Emily.

393
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,980
I know, I know, I know he does, but I have to tell him how I feel.

394
00:20:41,150 --> 00:20:45,450
He deserves to have all of the information. Then he can make an informed decision.

395
00:20:45,610 --> 00:20:48,820
That's not why you're going. You're going because you hope he'll say:

396
00:20:48,990 --> 00:20:52,790
"Yeah, I love you too, Rach. Forget about that British chippie."

397
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,210
Do you think he will?

398
00:20:55,370 --> 00:20:59,170
No, because he's in love with the British chippie.

399
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:04,720
Look, Rachel, if you go, you're just gonna mess with his head and ruin his wedding.

400
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:07,510
You know? It's too late. You missed your chance.

401
00:21:08,470 --> 00:21:10,470
I'm sorry. I know this must be really hard.

402
00:21:12,350 --> 00:21:14,140
But it's over.

403
00:21:17,650 --> 00:21:20,940
You know what? No. It's not over until someone says "I do."

404
00:21:21,690 --> 00:21:24,690
I do. I do! I do!

405
00:21:30,450 --> 00:21:33,790
Yeah, like I can really chase you. I'm carrying a litter.

